---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Terms of Use | Unroot Design';
const description = 'Terms of use for unroot.design: project assets, payments, the Concept, trial and monthly work, refunds and ownership.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <header class="phead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="tag"><i></i>Legal</p>
      <h1 class="h1">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="lede mono legal__date">Last updated: 19 September 2026</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose legal">

      <p>By working with Unroot Design or using this website, you agree to the terms below.</p>

      <h2>1. Project assets and storage</h2>
      <p>Once a project is complete, all requested assets are delivered and final payment is received, we keep your files (Figma designs, development versions, 3D files, images) available for 30 days. Ask us before that window closes and we will happily extend it.</p>
      <p>In practice we keep our work in Figma and rarely delete anything, but we are not obliged to store it, and once a project is finished we are not responsible for what happens to those files afterwards. Download everything you need and keep your own copy.</p>

      <h2>2. Outsourcing and team</h2>
      <p>We may bring in contractors for parts of your project unless an NDA says otherwise. We stay responsible for quality and delivery either way.</p>

      <h2>3. Payments</h2>
      <p>We require an upfront payment and a final payment on completion. We accept Stripe, crypto, Wise and bank transfer.</p>

      <h2>4. The Concept</h2>
      <p>The Concept is a fixed deliverable: 1 animated, interactive homepage direction, designed in Figma and vibe coded into a live preview, delivered within 7 days of payment. It does not include revisions. The amount paid is credited toward a full redesign if you start one within 60 days. You keep the concept file either way and may build from it yourself, but you may not resell it.</p>

      <h2>5. Trial week and monthly work</h2>
      <p>A trial week covers 5 working days. Monthly work runs in 4 week blocks and can be paused or ended before the next block starts. Work already delivered inside a block is not refundable.</p>

      <h2>6. Project start</h2>
      <p>Your project officially starts when the first payment is made, or on the start date we agree in writing.</p>

      <h2>7. Client inactivity</h2>
      <p>If we do not hear from you for 2 months, we treat the project as closed and completed unless we have agreed otherwise. We are not obliged to deliver anything further after that.</p>

      <h2>8. Portfolio rights</h2>
      <p>We may show your project in our portfolio and on social media, including work in progress. If you would rather we wait until launch, tell us and we will.</p>

      <h2>9. Design changes</h2>
      <p>Once you approve a design and it has been developed, further changes need a new agreement or a new scope.</p>

      <h2>10. Scope adjustments</h2>
      <p>If we combine or adjust pages, for example merging two pages into one, that does not mean less work was done. Scope changes are part of the process.</p>

      <h2>11. Refunds</h2>
      <p>We do not give refunds. This is digital work: the hours go in the moment we start, and they cannot be taken back once they are spent.</p>
      <p>If you are not sure yet, that is exactly what the small steps are for. Start with <a href="/#concept">the Concept</a> or <a href="/#pricing">a trial week</a>, see how we work, and decide from there.</p>

      <h2>12. Liability and warranties</h2>
      <p>This website and our services are provided as they are. We are not liable for damages resulting from use of the website or from project outcomes.</p>

      <h2>13. Account responsibility</h2>
      <p>You are responsible for managing your account and billing details.</p>

      <h2>14. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>We can update these terms at any time. Continued use means you accept the changes.</p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>Write to <a href="mailto:adam@unroot.design">adam@unroot.design</a> anytime.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal__date { color: var(--ink-3); }
</style>
